local _, ns = ...

ns.MapChangelog = {
	{ version = "Unreleased", date = "", heads = { [1] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aZooming in notch by notch is smooth again|r: since 0.8.1 the blur came back all at once each time the map stopped, one long frame the next wheel notch landed on. It now waits out a pause between notches and comes back a few zones a frame. Questie's mob paths are worked out once the map stops, not on every frame of a zoom.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.8.1", date = "2026-11-08", heads = { [1] = "New", [3] = "Improved", [6] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aQuestie's mob paths on the stitched map|r, drawn over the art for the zones near the view as you zoom in (Questie's own were under the art, and only on the zone's own map).",
		"|cff6e2c0aDarkening colour|r (Options, under Darkening): the colour unexplored areas are darkened with, picked with the game's colour picker; |cff6e2c0aDefault colour|r brings back the dark one.",
		"|cff6e2c0aZooming is about four times smoother|r: OpenMap no longer lays out its hidden icons and its blur on every frame of a zoom (the blur comes back a moment after you stop). Found and measured by Peendars.",
		"|cff6e2c0aFlight masters are easier to see on the map|r: bigger, with a dark outline, and the ones you haven't learned are no longer half see-through (they were lost on the parchment).",
		"|cff6e2c0aCtrl-click drops a pin can be turned off|r (Options, and the menu's More tab): with Map Pin Enhanced a Ctrl-click dropped two pins, its own and OpenMap's. Off, the menu's Drop a pin still works.",
		"|cff6e2c0aQuestie's icons show the first time you open the map|r: after a login they could be missing until the map was closed and opened again (Questie was still setting up when OpenMap looked).",
		"|cff6e2c0aZygor's waypoint shows on the stitched map|r, in the right place and over the art (Zygor uses its own renamed copy of HereBeDragons, which OpenMap didn't know). Traced by robnoord.",
		"|cff6e2c0aYour class's trainers are found on every language's client|r: on a French client (and the other non-English ones) every class trainer showed as a profession trainer.",
		"|cff6e2c0aAn NPC who walks about shows once on the map|r: Girl with Puppies in Orgrimmar had a vendor icon at every point of her walk, dozens over the city. An NPC with many spawns in one zone (with Vendors and the other townsfolk on) now has one icon, in the middle of where it walks. Fixed by diegodiaz1256.",
		"|cff6e2c0aNo friends dot or badge for yourself|r: with Share where you are on, you could show on your own map as a guild member (the guild's roster can spell your realm differently).",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map opens at once inside a dungeon|r: each opening loaded the dungeon's map art again, a second or two (longer in dungeons with many floors, whose Floors tab shows every floor). OpenMap now keeps the art of the dungeon you're in loaded, as it does the world map's.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.8.0-beta", date = "2026-11-07", heads = { [1] = "New", [2] = "Improved", [4] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aFriends and guild on the map|r (Options: Friends and guild): your guild members and friends on your realm who are online show on the stitched map, a badge on the zone each is in with who's there. Those who use OpenMap and turn on |cff6e2c0aShare where you are|r show as a class-coloured dot where they stand, updated every few seconds while they move. The map asks once whether to share; it's off unless you say yes, goes only to your guild and your friends, and never from inside a dungeon, raid or battleground.",
		"|cff6e2c0aA new OpenMap icon, drawn by zloyeb|r: a map scroll in a gold ring, in the AddOns list, on the minimap button, in the map's menu and its portrait (it borrowed the game's Eastern Kingdoms icon).",
		"|cff6e2c0aOpenMap is back on GitHub|r, at github.com/openmap-world/openmap: Report a problem opens a report there again, and What's new and the AddOns list link to it.",
		"|cff6e2c0a\"Center on player, keep zoom\" opens at your zoom straight away|r: having moved since the map closed, it opened on the zone's whole map for a moment and then jumped to the zoom kept.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map opens with its art already there|r: the game let go of the map's art while it was closed, and each opening loaded it again (blank parchment for a moment). OpenMap now keeps it loaded while the map is closed; /openmap warm turns that off.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map closes in combat again|r: with the map open as a fight started, neither Escape nor M closed it (since 0.7.0). The windowed map no longer stays open beside an NPC's window, which is what blocked it.",
		"|cff6e2c0aFlight masters you haven't learned show as not learned|r: some showed as learned, as OpenMap counted the stops a flight passes through. What it remembered is forgotten once and counted again at the next flight master you talk to.",
		"|cff6e2c0aFlight masters are named in your own language|r: on a client that isn't English, the map's flight masters kept the game's tables' English names. They're now named as the game names them, and a flight's measured time is found again on a route.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map window can't go above the top of the screen|r, where its title bar couldn't be grabbed to bring it back. /openmap reset puts the window back to its size and place.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe OpenMap menu fits a short screen|r: on a TV at a big UI scale the Look tab ran off the bottom.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.7.1-beta", date = "2026-10-21", heads = { [1] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map loads the zone you pan or zoom to again|r: with an addon adding map icons, it could stay on the zone you started on, so the zone you'd panned to showed none of their icons until you clicked it. Its setting, once Follow the view, is now |cff6e2c0aLoad the zone in view|r.",
		"|cff6e2c0aFlight masters you've learned are in colour|r, all of them: OpenMap knew only the ones it had seen you visit since it was installed (and, on a client not in English, none). It now asks the game which you've found.",
		"|cff6e2c0aRetail: your arrow and the map's icons where they are in the cities|r: in Stormwind, your arrow, Blizzard's flight master and the other icons on the city's map were drawn tens of yards from where they are (a player's report).",
		"|cff6e2c0aWith Enhance QoL|r, OpenMap says once in chat to turn off its Mover > World Map: the two both size the map, and its scale goes wrong (a player's finding).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.7.0-beta", date = "2026-10-20", heads = { [1] = "New", [2] = "Improved", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aOpenMap for retail|r (Midnight): the same seamless map, from retail's own maps. Every continent on Azeroth's map, its zones stitched in as you zoom with their explored areas painted (or hidden until you've been there, as Blizzard's own map does), Blizzard's art as it is; the world's parchment out to its torn edge and on past it; dungeon and raid entrances from the encounter journal with every floor of their maps, flight masters, boats and zeppelins, the close-up minimap. A download of its own on CurseForge.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map stays open while you talk to an NPC|r (or open a vendor, the bags' windows ...): the windowed map is no longer put away to make room. Escape still closes it; maximized, it behaves as before.",
		"|cff6e2c0aReopen map: Center on player, keep zoom|r (the menu's Reopen map, and Options): the map opens on you at the zoom you closed it at.",
		"|cff6e2c0aChoose your map|r: the choice the first time the map opens is in the map window's own frame, with plainer words.",
		"|cff6e2c0aA little lighter at the whole-world view|r: a city's map isn't drawn at all until it starts to fade in (before, it was drawn unseen).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.5.0-beta", date = "2026-10-16", heads = { [1] = "New", [12] = "Improved", [18] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aKhaz Modan's blank land painted|r: the stretches between Dun Morogh, Wetlands, Loch Modan, Searing Gorge and the Badlands that no zone map covers, and the coast round them, painted by hand by Santiago Reyes in the zone maps' own style, from Blizzard's art and following the game's terrain (used with his permission). The first of the gaps between zones to be filled; Options' |cff6e2c0aFilled gaps|r turns them off.",
		"|cff6e2c0aMaps of City of Dalaran and Excavation Site: Wetlands|r, drawn by Santiago Reyes and used with his permission: click their entrances in Alterac Mountains and the Wetlands (they opened on a blank page before). \"Map by Santiago Reyes\" at their foot, as with his others.",
		"|cff6e2c0aAirships to Zephras Isle|r: the flying boats at the Dalaran skydock (Alterac Mountains) and in Mulgore are on the map; click one and Zephras Isle's map opens in the window, as a dungeon's does, and Back takes you to the world where you were. (Under the Boats switch.)",
		"|cff6e2c0aMaps of Ruins of Lordaeron and The Hall of Thanes|r, two of WoW Forever's own dungeons, which the game has no map of: drawn by Santiago Reyes and used with his permission. Click their entrances in Undercity and Ironforge; the map shows \"Map by Santiago Reyes\" at its foot.",
		"|cff6e2c0aDungeon Journal|r: with Exehn's Dungeon Journal installed, a dungeon's map has |cff6e2c0aOpen in Dungeon Journal|r on its Bosses tab, and clicking an entrance can open its page there instead of its map (the menu's |cff6e2c0aEntrances open Dungeon Journal|r, or Options). Its map still opens where Dungeon Journal has no page for it.",
		"|cff6e2c0aDungeon quests without Questie|r: the Quests tab works with Dungeon Journal or NeedRoll too, as a button that opens the dungeon's quests in it. With more than one installed, Options' |cff6e2c0aDungeon quests from|r picks which (the first installed: Questie, then Dungeon Journal, then NeedRoll).",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe OpenMap button off the map, if you like|r: |cff6e2c0aOpenMap button on the map|r (the menu's Look tab) hides it and the favourites. The menu is still a click away: OpenMap is in the minimap's AddOns list, and there's a |cff6e2c0aminimap button|r if you want one (the Look tab, or Options). Click for the map and its menu, right-click for the options window, drag it round the minimap; /openmap works too.",
		"|cff6e2c0aA choice the first time the map opens|r on a new install: |cff6e2c0aClassic|r (unexplored areas hidden, no dungeon or flight master icons, no zone levels, the favourite buttons folded away) or |cff6e2c0aOpenMap|r (as it comes). Settings you already have aren't asked about or changed; /openmap welcome asks again. Suggested in #24.",
		"|cff6e2c0aYour arrow on top, or off|r: the player arrow is drawn over every other icon on the map (quest givers, Questie's and other addons' icons), so you can always see which way you're facing (suggested in #31); your party's markers come up with it. Or take it off the world map (the menu's Show tab, |cff6e2c0aYour arrow|r) and find your way old-school by the land around you: your party still shows, and so does the minimap.",
		"|cff6e2c0aIcons from zoom|r: a slider (the menu's Look tab, or Options) for the zoom the icons for places (dungeons, boats, zeppelins and flight masters) show from: 1x has them from the whole world, higher keeps the map clean further out. Auto, as before, brings each in at its own zoom. Townsfolk never come in further out than their own; your pins, drawings and party always show.",
		"OpenMap shows under a |cff6e2c0aMap|r category in the game's AddOns list.",
		"|cff6e2c0aMap frame rate cap|r (the menu's Look tab, or Options; off unless you set it): the frame rate at most while the map is open. A big map draws many layers over the whole screen every frame; at 60 the graphics card does about half the work it does at 120 (reported: a full-screen 4K map doubling the card's power). Your own frame rate setting comes back as the map closes.",
		"Up close, a layer of the paper grain that has faded out is no longer drawn.",
		"|cff6e2c0aReport a problem|r sends you to OpenMap's comments on CurseForge for now, to post its code in (What's new's link goes to OpenMap's CurseForge page too). Its window, and the bench's and the map notes' to copy from, are in the map window's own frame.",
		"|cff6e2c0aDungeons, boats and zeppelins each have their own switch|r in the menu's Show tab and in Options, so you can keep dungeon and raid entrances and hide the boats or zeppelins. A kind that's off takes its routes with it when routes are shown. Your old setting carries over to all three.",
		"|cff6e2c0aOut of a city to its zone|r: right-click out of Stormwind, Ironforge, Darnassus, Orgrimmar, Thunder Bluff or Undercity and the map goes out to the zone around it (Elwynn Forest, Dun Morogh ...), as it does from anywhere else in that zone, not the whole continent.",
		"|cff6e2c0aAzeroth Tripview|r: its live ships and docks are kept above the map's art. For other addons, OpenMapAPI (version 2) can now place a point of the game's world anywhere on the stitched map, for frames they put on the world map themselves (docs/api.md).",
		"Zooming in quickly, the zones no longer flicker to blank parchment for a moment: the map's pre-drawn tiles now stay until every zone coming into view has its art in.",
		"Opening a dungeon's map no longer can raise a Lua error the first time (when the map window changed size as it opened, as in full screen).",
		"|cff6e2c0aWith a gamepad|r: the cursor stays where you put it. It jumped back to the middle of the map each time the map underneath changed (shortly after every zoom or pan), so the next zoom was about the middle. And in combat, a dungeon's or Zephras Isle's map waits until you're out of it (a line in chat says so): opened then, the game set the map's gamepad buttons again in a way it blocks in combat, which could leave them wrong until a /reload.",
		"|cff6e2c0aWoW Forever's boats|r are on the map, with their docks and routes: Steamwheedle Port (Tanaris) to Powderfuse Port (Riverglades), for both factions; Stormwind to Auberdine; and Menethil Harbor to Southshore and Auberdine, which takes the place of the old Menethil to Auberdine boat.",
		"|cff6e2c0aWoW Forever's flight masters|r: Farholde Keep and Powderfuse Port for the Alliance, Rog'mar and Powderfuse Port for the Horde, with their flights (Farholde Keep to Powderfuse Port, Lakeshire, Morgan's Vigil and Thelsamar; Rog'mar to Stonard, Kargath, Flame Crest and Hammerfall). The flight network now comes from WoW Forever's own tables, which have moved Stormwind's flight master and redrawn some of the classic flights.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe close-up minimap on towns by the sea and on islands|r: Menethil Harbor, Southshore, Theramore, Booty Bay's shallows, Teldrassil and Darnassus, Feathermoon Stronghold. It was cut to the continent map's coarse outline of the land, which leaves out what that map draws as sea; it now takes in each zone map's own land too.",
		"|cff6e2c0aNo retail Eversong Woods or Zul'Aman over Quel'Thalas|r: the minimap is now only the tiles the game itself draws (those its own world map file lists), which also leaves out other versions' sea far west of Dun Morogh and east of Wetlands, and the Draenei isles off Kalimdor.",
		"Blizzard's classic maps drawn in the land between zones are placed where WoW Forever places those zones. They were placed by Mists of Pandaria Classic's tables, whose zones are Cataclysm's, so The Barrens' was drawn at Northern Barrens' size and Stonetalon Mountains', Silithus', Badlands', Dun Morogh's and Azshara's were off, showing copies of their mountains beside the real ones. Cataclysm's Hillsbrad Foothills (Alterac taken in) and a different drawing of Mulgore are no longer used.",
		"The cave maps of four places WoW Forever doesn't have are gone: Greymane Manor (Gilneas), Spitescale Cavern (the Echo Isles as Cataclysm remade them), and Legion's Keeper's Rest and Karazhan Catacombs.",
		"|cff6e2c0aBooks on Map Forever|r's book icons show on the stitched map: they were drawn under its art. Which ones show is still the addon's own choice (those of the zone or continent the map is on).",
		"The zone you're looking at has its name over the map again when you hover it, where the game names no place in it (Silverpine Forest's had gone; reported in #25). With Zone levels off, zone names still show, without their levels.",
		"|cff6e2c0aMove Any|r owns the map window: with it, OpenMap's title bar, resize grips and saved place stand down, so Move Any's own drag and resize work on the map again (reported in #23). The map size slider and Reset size and place are off then.",
		"A city's own map that went missing (Ironforge showing only Dun Morogh's painting of it, until a /reload: reported in #30) is shown again when you reopen the map, and the map's check of what's in view no longer stays stuck if it stopped part way. (A safeguard: what hid it isn't known yet.)",
	} },
}
